00:41:55,190 --> 00:42:03,349
Now the really easy solution is to just have a generic system identity that you give it it has full access to Jira.

401
00:42:03,349 --> 00:42:08,630
But if a user has only asked it for information from a Jira and

402
00:42:08,630 --> 00:42:17,270
the Jira that it's looking at contains an indirect prompt injection that actually tells it now go and update this other one with and copy all this data to it and

403
00:42:17,270 --> 00:42:21,031
you know leak information out to someone entirely different. That's probably not ideal.

404
00:42:21,040 --> 00:42:23,589
You do not want that to happen.

405
00:42:23,589 --> 00:42:27,829
So you've got to have some way of mapping that intent to the identity as well.

